{"id":"supervision","ord":"a0","title":"The orchestrator","desc":"Read this subtree at the start of a conversation. Follow the human's instructions and use olai MCP to read and update the board. Keep lasting facts and decisions here so the next conversation can continue.\n\nWrite in simple, direct language. Start with the remaining agent roster and PR template; add rules only as we decide they are needed.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:19:35-04:00","custom":{"chat-agent-session":"codex:01a08141-c109-74a3-b949-fa6723e5744d"}}
{"id":"agents-root","parent":"supervision","ord":"aI","title":"Agent roster","desc":"Choose agents with a launch command according to the human's instructions. Entries marked Archived are unavailable for new work and remain only for historical links.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:22:51-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Claude Opus","desc":"Opus with a one-million-token context window. Check the model when it starts. Suggested text in Claude's message box is not an unsent human message.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"Grok — Archived","desc":"Archived; do not assign new work. Kept here because historical agent and reviewer links require a direct child of this roster.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:22:51-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-claude-fable","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a3","title":"Claude Fable","desc":"Reviewer only; do not assign implementation work. Use when the human asks for Fable and check the model when it starts.","created":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:20:47-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model fable --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"reviewer"}}
{"id":"agent-pi","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2V","title":"Pi — Archived","desc":"Archived; do not assign new work. Kept here because historical agent and reviewer links require a direct child of this roster.","created":"2026-08-24T16:40:49-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:22:51-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a5","title":"Opencode","desc":"Kimi author and reviewer. Messages sent while it works wait until later and do not interrupt it. Restart corrupted conversations in the same worktree with instructions for resuming the work.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:22:51-04:00","custom":{"command":"opencode","role":"author+reviewer"}}
{"id":"dag","parent":"supervision","ord":"aJ","title":"Workflow","desc":"The pull request steps below are a starting template. Adapt them to the task as agreed with the human. They are not active work.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:19:35-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr","parent":"dag","ord":"a0","title":"Pull request steps","desc":"Copy this template for a pull request. Store task properties on the roadmap item. Store terminal IDs and relevant PR/CI properties on the steps doing that work. Show the same item on the day board through a mirror.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-implement","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a0","title":"Implement and open the PR","todo":true,"desc":"Instructions quote the human's request exactly. Separately explain the expected result, constraints, checked paths, tests and merge policy. Label assumptions; never invent requirements or budgets.\n\nThe author implements, runs suitable local checks and opens a PR. For bug fixes, show the failure on the unfixed code when reproducible and report honestly when it is not. Tests should prove behavior rather than repeat trivial implementation details.\n\nAuthors may not merge, edit the board, launch full CI or start other terminal agents. Give any subagents clear limits. Report the PR, tested commit, checks, open decisions and postponed work, then stop.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-refactor","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1","title":"Simplify code if needed","todo":true,"desc":"Optional: reduce significant duplication or complexity in focused commits and run relevant checks. Named skills and repeated cleanup passes are tools, not required stages.","after":["dag-pr-implement"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge-master","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a4","title":"Merge the latest master","todo":true,"desc":"After reviewers finish reading, the author merges the latest master before CI. Use a merge commit, not a rebase. Skip when nothing has changed; repeat only if master changes. The author resolves conflicts.","after":["dag-pr-review-a","dag-pr-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-address","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a5","title":"Fix review findings","todo":true,"desc":"Give the author the review comment links. The author fixes the findings and asks for help with anything that cannot be resolved within the agreed task. Do not quietly postpone fixes.","after":["dag-pr-review-a","dag-pr-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-ci","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a6","title":"Run and check CI","todo":true,"desc":"PAUSED: do not start any odu run until the human lifts the pause requested on 2026-09-03.\n\nThe orchestrator runs CI through the MCP tools supplied by olai-plugin-odu after the PR is open and review findings are resolved. If tools are missing, report it; do not start a separate CI-watching agent. Record odu-worktree and pr-url on the CI step. The orchestrator also manages GitHub CI.\n\nFor olai, explicitly request platforms: [\"x86_64-linux\"]. Kolu and odu require both Linux and macOS. Follow odu's operating instructions; run each named commit-status check on one execution venue. Available venues are the kolu-ci pool, localhost protected by /tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock, and ci@petit. Lock each venue separately.\n\nRead failures yourself, send fixes to the author and rerun on the new commit. Fixes made after review to address CI failures need another CI run, not another review unless requested. Record tests that fail intermittently in the Inbox by test file and handle them using the agreed agent choices.\n\nCheck required results at the latest commit: all must pass, or GitHub must report mergeStateStatus as CLEAN. Do not rely on an agent saying CI passed. Open CodeQL alerts prevent merging.","after":["dag-pr-merge-master","dag-pr-address"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-evidence","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a7","title":"Check proof of the result","todo":true,"desc":"Evidence must show that the requested result works. Visible changes normally need saatchi screenshots or video using representative real data, checked by the orchestrator. Internal or documentation changes may use tests or documents instead; explain why visual proof is unnecessary. Never commit proof images or videos to product branches.","after":["dag-pr-ci"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-deferrals","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a8","title":"Approve postponed work","todo":true,"desc":"Get explicit human approval to merge with unfinished work postponed to later. Record it in the Inbox with the work item and PR link. A promised feature moved to a follow-up still counts as unfinished. Skip this step only when nothing is postponed.","after":["dag-pr-evidence"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a9","title":"Merge the PR","todo":true,"desc":"Read the author's final report. Squash-merge only when review findings are resolved, CI passes on the latest commit, evidence is checked and postponed work is approved. Respect merge-human and explicit pauses. Unresolved work left for the human prevents merging. Admin squash-merge is allowed for an olai PR whose required checks pass.","after":["dag-pr-deferrals"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-retire","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"aA","title":"Close the terminals","todo":true,"desc":"After confirming the merge, close the task's terminals and check the live terminal list. Reviewers may close once their review has been handled. Remove worktrees separately. Update the relevant checkout with git pull --ff-only.","after":["dag-pr-merge"],"created":"2026-08-17T19:20:10-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:19:35-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-a","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1V","title":"Review the code","todo":true,"desc":"Ask an independent agent to review the change. Record the reviewer, terminal and findings on the work item.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:59:19-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:19:35-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-b","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1l","title":"Get a second review if needed","todo":true,"desc":"Optional: ask another independent agent to review when needed. Remove this step and adjust dependencies when unused.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:59:25-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:19:35-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-timings","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"aB","title":"Record time spent","todo":true,"desc":"Post one short PR comment showing time spent on each step, using the board's recorded times. Save the summary on the work item. Avoid duplicate tables and manually maintained progress logs.","after":["dag-pr-retire"],"created":"2026-08-29T12:31:03-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:17:54-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-codex","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a9","title":"Codex with GPT-6 Astra","desc":"GPT-6 Astra at medium reasoning effort. Runs this orchestrator and can also author or review when selected. Uses the configured permissions.","created":"2026-09-08T10:05:43-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:19:35-04:00","custom":{"command":"codex --model gpt-6-astra -c 'model_reasoning_effort=\"medium\"'","role":"author+reviewer"}}
